Feature: Compound Drug Analysis Aggregation and Categorization

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.compound_drug_analysis" in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks"
    And the table contains columns: study_id, compound_id, mutation_id, therapeutic_area, drug_name, ic50, auc, efficacy, toxicity, potency, sample_size, mutation_frequency, mutation_severity, compound_concentration, cell_viability, growth_inhibition, result, approved_flag, validation_status, status, created_by, score1, score2, score3, score4, score5

  Scenario: Filter and aggregate compound drug analysis data by therapeutic area
    Given the table contains valid data for all required columns
    When the dataset is filtered to include only rows where approved_flag = 1 and validation_status = 'valid'
    And the filtered data is grouped by therapeutic_area to calculate:
      | metric             | calculation                        |
      | avg_ic50           | average(ic50)                      |
      | avg_auc            | average(auc)                       |
      | avg_efficacy       | average(efficacy)                  |
      | total_sample_size  | sum(sample_size)                   |
      | study_count        | countDistinct(study_id)            |
    Then the aggregated metrics are joined to each filtered row on therapeutic_area
    And for each row, overall_score is computed as average(score1, score2, score3, score4, score5)
    And each row is categorized into potential_category:
      | condition                          | category           |
      | overall_score >= 70 and <= 100     | High Potential     |
      | overall_score >= 60 and < 70       | Moderate Potential |
      | overall_score < 60                 | Low Potential      |
    And the final output includes all original columns, aggregated metrics, overall_score, and potential_category

  Scenario Outline: Categorization of compound results by overall_score
    Given a filtered row with score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When overall_score is calculated as average of the five scores
    Then the row is categorized as <potential_category>

    Examples:
      | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 | overall_score | potential_category   |
      | 80     | 85     | 90     | 75     | 80     | 82            | High Potential      |
      | 65     | 62     | 68     | 66     | 64     | 65            | Moderate Potential  |
      | 55     | 58     | 59     | 57     | 56     | 57            | Low Potential       |
      | 100    | 100    | 100    | 100    | 100    | 100           | High Potential      |
      | 70     | 70     | 70     | 70     | 70     | 70            | High Potential      |
      | 69     | 69     | 69     | 69     | 69     | 69            | Moderate Potential  |
      | 60     | 60     | 60     | 60     | 60     | 60            | Moderate Potential  |
      | 59     | 59     | 59     | 59     | 59     | 59            | Low Potential       |
      | 0      | 0      | 0      | 0      | 0      | 0             | Low Potential       |
      | 75     | 80     | 85     | 90     | 95     | 85            | High Potential      |

  Scenario Outline: Aggregation metrics per therapeutic_area
    Given filtered rows for therapeutic_area <therapeutic_area>
    When aggregation is performed
    Then the following metrics are calculated:
      | avg_ic50         | <avg_ic50>         |
      | avg_auc          | <avg_auc>          |
      | avg_efficacy     | <avg_efficacy>     |
      | total_sample_size| <total_sample_size>|
      | study_count      | <study_count>      |

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | avg_ic50 | avg_auc | avg_efficacy | total_sample_size | study_count |
      | Oncology        | 0.5      | 0.8     | 0.7          | 1000              | 5           |
      | Cardiology      | 1.2      | 1.0     | 0.9          | 800               | 3           |
      | Neurology       | 0.7      | 0.6     | 0.5          | 1200              | 7           |
      | Immunology      | 0.9      | 0.7     | 0.8          | 950               | 4           |
      | Endocrinology   | 1.1      | 1.2     | 1.0          | 1100              | 6           |

  Scenario Outline: Filtering rows by approved_flag and validation_status
    Given a row with approved_flag=<approved_flag> and validation_status=<validation_status>
    When filtering is applied
    Then the row is <included_or_excluded> in the analysis

    Examples:
      | approved_flag | validation_status | included_or_excluded |
      | 1             | valid             | included            |
      | 0             | valid             | excluded            |
      | 1             | invalid           | excluded            |
      | 0             | invalid           | excluded            |
      | 1             | VALID             | excluded            |
      | 1             | Valid             | excluded            |
      | 1             | valid             | included            |
      | null          | valid             | excluded            |
      | 1             | null              | excluded            |
      | null          | null              | excluded            |

  Scenario Outline: Join filtered data with aggregated metrics
    Given a filtered row with therapeutic_area=<therapeutic_area>
    And aggregated metrics exist for <therapeutic_area>
    When the join is performed
    Then the row contains the following additional columns:
      | avg_ic50         | <avg_ic50>         |
      | avg_auc          | <avg_auc>          |
      | avg_efficacy     | <avg_efficacy>     |
      | total_sample_size| <total_sample_size>|
      | study_count      | <study_count>      |

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | avg_ic50 | avg_auc | avg_efficacy | total_sample_size | study_count |
      | Oncology        | 0.5      | 0.8     | 0.7          | 1000              | 5           |
      | Cardiology      | 1.2      | 1.0     | 0.9          | 800               | 3           |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing or invalid score values
    Given a filtered row with score1=<score1>, score2=<score2>, score3=<score3>, score4=<score4>, score5=<score5>
    When overall_score is computed
    Then if any score is missing or not a number, overall_score is null and potential_category is "Unknown"
    And an error message "Missing or invalid score value(s) for study_id <study_id>" is logged

    Examples:
      | score1 | score2 | score3 | score4 | score5 | study_id | overall_score | potential_category |
      | 80     | 85     | null   | 75     | 80     | S001     | null          | Unknown           |
      | 65     | 'abc'  | 68     | 66     | 64     | S002     | null          | Unknown           |
      | null   | null   | null   | null   | null   | S003     | null          | Unknown           |
      | 70     | 70     | 70     | 70     | 70     | S004     | 70            | High Potential    |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing therapeutic_area in join
    Given a filtered row with therapeutic_area=<therapeutic_area>
    And no aggregated metrics exist for <therapeutic_area>
    When the join is performed
    Then the row contains null for aggregated metrics
    And an error message "No aggregated metrics found for therapeutic_area <therapeutic_area>" is logged

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | avg_ic50 | avg_auc | avg_efficacy | total_sample_size | study_count |
      | UnknownArea     | null     | null    | null         | null              | null        |
      | Oncology        | 0.5      | 0.8     | 0.7          | 1000              | 5           |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for duplicate study_id in aggregation
    Given multiple rows with the same study_id and therapeutic_area
    When aggregation is performed
    Then study_count is calculated as count of distinct study_id per therapeutic_area

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | study_ids         | study_count |
      | Oncology        | S001,S002,S001    | 2           |
      | Cardiology      | S003,S004,S005    | 3           |

  Scenario Outline: Data type validation for approved_flag
    Given a row with approved_flag=<approved_flag>
    When filtering is applied
    Then if approved_flag is not an integer, the row is excluded and error "Invalid approved_flag type for study_id <study_id>" is logged

    Examples:
      | approved_flag | study_id | included_or_excluded |
      | 1             | S001     | included            |
      | '1'           | S002     | excluded            |
      | null          | S003     | excluded            |
      | 0             | S004     | excluded            |

  Scenario: Final output columns
    Given the filtered and joined data
    When the final output is generated
    Then the output includes all original columns from compound_drug_analysis
    And the following additional columns: avg_ic50, avg_auc, avg_efficacy, total_sample_size, study_count, overall_score, potential_category

# END
